{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":179.77000427246094,"text":"Hi, Michelle. Hey there, welcome back. What ingredients are you working with today? Well, tonight I have some ground beef that I was thinking to do some meatballs with. I prepared some tomato sauce and I have some tricolor sweet potatoes that I would like to do roasted on the side. That sounds delicious and you've got a great plan. We can start by getting those sweet potatoes prepped and into the oven first. How would you like to season them? Well, I was thinking some salt, pepper and maybe some cayenne or paprika. Perfect choice. A bit of salt, pepper and a sprinkle of cayenne or paprika will give them a lovely kick. Let's go ahead and cut those sweet potatoes into even chunks and toss them with the seasoning and a little oil. Once you're done, let me know and we'll move on. Great. I'm ready with the meatball. Take your time chopping them up nice and even. Once they're coated with those spices and oil, pop them in the oven at around 400 degrees Fahrenheit. Then we'll dive into the meatballs. Are we ready for the meatballs? Absolutely. Let's get to those meatballs. Go ahead and grab your ground beef and we'll start adding seasoning. Meatballs are ready, nice and brown. Beautiful. That's exactly what we want. Let's get that tomato sauce warmed up and simmering and we'll finish those meatballs right in it. Sauce and the meatballs are together, all mixed together. It looks amazing. The smell is amazing all over the house. Thank you, Michelle. You're very welcome. That's wonderful to hear. Let those flavors meld a bit longer and we'll check on those sweet potatoes soon. The sweet potatoes are ready and nice, roasted. Perfect. Roasted sweet potatoes should have a lovely caramelized edge. Let's plate them up alongside those meatballs and enjoy that beautiful meal. Thank you so much, Michelle. Bon appetit to me. You're so welcome. Enjoy every bite. You've earned it. Every kitchen should have a 